 ## Overview
-The Secant Method for Surface Depth Refinement is an iterative root-finding algorithm used to refine the depth value $d$ along a ray where a signed distance function (SDF) or occupancy logit crosses a specific threshold [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of locating the precise zero-crossing of a scalar field by using linear interpolation between two bracketing points to estimate the next candidate point [S1, unofficial]. Not given in the sources.
